course: dictionary
lesson: 9150
title: Snobbish and looking down on others
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A snob thinks they are better than other people because they are richer, posher or more educated, and looks down on them. Snobbish is the describing word: a snobbish person, or a snobbish attitude. The words around it give you the clues.
explain: «The social gulf between them was so very wide» is a clue. Toad is rich and the gaoler's daughter is not, so he thinks he is above her. Swap in your meaning: "Toad thinks he is better than her because of his money" still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Snobbish words are often rude. «I will not be laughed at by a bargewoman!» shows how people use insults like «common» to hurt someone. Toad is friendly too, so snobbish is one part of his character, not all of it.
explain: A snob can look down on a country way of talking, but every accent and dialect is fine. Being snobbish is never kind, whatever someone's money or family.
fact: Snobbish means thinking you are better than other people and looking down on them.
fact: A snob is a person who acts this way, and snobbery is the behaviour or idea itself.
fact: «A snobbish attitude» means a proud, looking-down-on-others way of thinking.
fact: «Food snob» means someone who looks down on other people's food because they think their own tastes are better.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad can be snobbish about his grand house and money, though he is friendly too.
exercise: «The social gulf between them was so very wide.» What does this suggest about Toad? | He is lost in a wide field | He feels cold | *He thinks he is above the gaoler's daughter because he is richer | He is very tall
exercise: Which word means thinking you are better than other people and looking down on them? | gentle | kind | *snobbish | cheerful
exercise: Nadia says «snobbish» means being very tall. What does it really mean? | Losing things often | Shouting at a crowd | Being tall and thin | *Thinking you are better than others because of money or class
test: Which is an example of a snobbish attitude? | Saying hello to new classmates | Thanking the bus driver | *Saying someone's accent is common, so they are not as good as you | Sharing your sweets at break
test: Why is being snobbish unkind? | It only happens in old stories | It makes you grow taller | *It makes people feel small and ignores that everyone deserves respect | It means you know lots of words
exam: Toad is friendly and also snobbish, so what is the best description? | *Both can be true of one person, because people are often a mix of good and bad | He is never snobbish | He is never friendly | Friendly and snobbish mean exactly the same thing
